        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "on.pull_request.paths is removed; the first step (id: changes) lists PR files via gh api and writes a site output; the only later step is gated with if: steps.changes.outputs.site == 'true', so a docs-only PR skips the work and the job still succeeds, satisfying the required check. Script is sound (set -euo pipefail, event-path PR number, no expression injection, read-only permissions). Minor: relies on gh/jq availability and PR files API token access, which is fine on ubuntu-latest for pull_request events."
      },
